# .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub reads this file to decide who must review a change. A pattern
# earlier in the file is overridden by a pattern that comes later, so the
# order matters: catch-alls at the top, specific rules below.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of any file matched here. This is
# advisory: no branch protection or ruleset on master requires a code-owner
# approval, so it does not block a merge. If no pattern matches, no review is
# requested (contrast with a '*' rule, which would request review on every PR
# including the smallest web tweak — not the convention we are codifying).
#
# Keep this file short: add a path only when its review bar really is
# "Oscar sees this before it merges". The rest of the review discipline
# stays as it is, as a convention.

